error[ffi_writable_parameter]: `p` of `w_schar` is declared `cstr`, and the header says `signed char *` — C does not promise to leave it alone
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-411-signed-char-is-refused.hero:17:22
     |
  17 |     function w_schar(p: cstr lent) -> i32  #~ ffi_writable_parameter
     |                      ^
  note: spec § 13: `s.cstr()` lends a `str` to C, and C writes back through a lend only where the binding is a `@` name. A header's pointer without `const` does not promise that: a C write through it changes the bytes of every value that shares the string, and on a literal's stops the program
  note: declare it `ptr` and give `w_schar` a buffer C owns, then read the result back
  fix (guess): declare it `ptr`
